At the University of Nevada, Reno, I served as a Graduate Assistant from August 2022 to May 2026, gaining extensive experience in undergraduate economics instruction. I served as instructor of record for more than six semesters, independently teaching Principles of Macroeconomics (ECON 103), Principles of Statistics I (ECON 261), and Math Camp. My teaching experience also includes serving as a teaching assistant for Principles of Microeconomics, Intermediate Microeconomics, Principles of Statistics, Health Economics, Labor Economics, and Mathematical Economics. These roles have allowed me to teach a broad range of economic concepts and quantitative methods to students with diverse academic backgrounds.
